! CODE V freeform-prism export : fold24_nd151_fov50_02_3fold_fit0.633_CLEAN
! dom_signature : T@A -> TIR@D -> TIR@B -> TIR@A -> T@B
! Frame: origin at the source, +Z along the input chief ray (engine frame rotated
!        by -47.151000 deg). CODE V Z=along-axis, Y=meridional, X=out of plane.
! Placement: absolute. Every surface DAR + THI 0, so one global frame and a
!            repeated physical face can share ONE vertex and ONE coefficient set.
! Sequential closure: 85.7% of the traced bundle follows this
!            surface list; the rest is not represented by this file.
!
! UNVERIFIED IN CODE V: the SPS XYP block and the C<j> coefficient spelling below.
!            Everything else uses constructs confirmed by a live run. The term
!            ORDER is confirmed independently (see export_freeform_codev.xy_terms).
! EXPECT: THI is 0 on every surface, because absolute placement is what lets a
!            repeated face share one coefficient set. CODE V may therefore draw the
!            faces as separate sheets rather than one solid block -- that is a
!            rendering consequence of THI 0, not a placement error. Judge this file
!            on the global coordinate listing and whether rays reach SI, not on
!            whether View Lens shows a prism.
LEN NEW
DIM M
WL 587.56
REF 1
! EPD is the bundle's cross-section PERPENDICULAR to its own direction. The engine
!   emits along a vertical segment of beam_w = 8.000 mm, so that cross-section is
!   beam_w*cos(aim) and it varies with field: -5.00:5.931  -3.75:5.8125  -2.50:5.6912  -1.25:5.5672  +0.00:5.4405  +1.25:5.3113  +2.50:5.1795  +3.75:5.0453  +5.00:4.9087
!   CODE V has one EPD for all fields, so this matches the engine at the centre
!   field only. Worth fixing at the source if it ever matters.
EPD 5.440548
YAN -5.000000 -3.750000 -2.500000 -1.250000 0.000000 1.250000 2.500000 3.750000 5.000000
! ---- constant-index model glass. The engine carries ONE index and never splits a
!      ray by wavelength, so this is monochromatic by construction, not by choice.
PRV
PWL 587.56
'FOLDN' 1.509300
END
SO 0 1e18
! ---- S1: real stop, in air, ahead of all optics and ON axis (the rotated frame
!      is what buys that: in the engine frame this stop is decentered by ray_y).
CIR S1 2.720274
STO S1
THI S1 0

! ---- S2: refract @ face A   incidence 16.896 deg
S -281.802517 0 'FOLDN'
ZDE S2 18.655774
YDE S2 -28.095187
ADE S2 22.798200
DAR S2
REY S2 5.7485
REX S2 3.7203
ADY S2 29.0097
! face A freeform. Zero coefficients == the arc this design was
! discovered with, so the starting trace is unchanged and every subsequent
! change is attributable to the optimiser.
SPS XYP S2
C3 S2 0.0   ! x^2
C7 S2 0.0   ! x^2*y
C9 S2 0.0   ! y^3
C10 S2 0.0   ! x^4
C12 S2 0.0   ! x^2*y^2
C14 S2 0.0   ! y^4
C16 S2 0.0   ! x^4*y
C18 S2 0.0   ! x^2*y^3
C20 S2 0.0   ! y^5
C21 S2 0.0   ! x^6
C23 S2 0.0   ! x^4*y^2
C25 S2 0.0   ! x^2*y^4
C27 S2 0.0   ! y^6

